{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And has not washed his hands in water.</b> The intent of Scripture is immersion of the body, and it should have said 'and has not washed (רחץ) his hands in water,' but it called immersion by the term שטיפה because immersion requires that there be nothing interposing, but rather that he rinse his entire body in the water with his hands, in the manner of (Leviticus 6:21) ״ומורק ושוטף במים״, (Jeremiah 47:2) ״לנחל שוטף״. <b>Rashi wrote</b>, of blessed memory: Scripture expressed the immersion of the zav's body in the language of washing hands, to teach you that concealed parts do not require the entry of water, but only a revealed member like the hands."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:28.169744164Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}